From 11d8982f824d52e8122c7aa732207ba66b8f23c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] vold: allow exFAT fsck up to 120 seconds

Large exFAT volumes can take longer than the generic 45-second timeout to
check. Give exFAT its own two-minute timeout while retaining the existing
timeout for VFAT and other callers.

This patch is based on the official LineageOS pdx235 build's
LineageOS/android_system_vold revision
11d8982f824d52e8122c7aa732207ba66b8f23c8 (lineage-24.0).

diff --git a/Utils.h b/Utils.h
--- a/Utils.h
+++ b/Utils.h
@@ -41,2 +41,3 @@
 static constexpr std::chrono::seconds kUntrustedFsckSleepTime(45);
+static constexpr std::chrono::seconds kUntrustedExfatFsckSleepTime(120);
 static constexpr std::chrono::seconds kUntrustedMountSleepTime(20);
diff --git a/fs/Exfat.cpp b/fs/Exfat.cpp
--- a/fs/Exfat.cpp
+++ b/fs/Exfat.cpp
@@ -47,2 +47,2 @@
-    int rc = ForkExecvpTimeout(cmd, kUntrustedFsckSleepTime, sFsckUntrustedContext);
+    int rc = ForkExecvpTimeout(cmd, kUntrustedExfatFsckSleepTime, sFsckUntrustedContext);
     if (rc == 0) {
